    "body": "I discussed this with @fantasai and @litherum f2f. Elika said the spec is currently in an inconsistent state, but Myles was interested in working on this, which probably involves fixing parts of both the Logical Properties spec and HTML.\n\nI think since browsers already use logical properties in their UA stylesheets, and there is implementor interest, it seems like a good time to work on this.\n\nA few tests to show there's some interop:\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4171\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4172\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4173\n\nNot interoperable:\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4174\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4175\n\nUA stylesheets:\nhttps://github.com/WebKit/webkit/blob/master/Source/WebCore/css/html.css\nhttps://github.com/WebKit/webkit/blob/master/Source/WebCore/css/quirks.css\nhttps://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/css/html.css\nhttps://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/css/quirks.css\nhttp://mxr.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/source/layout/style/res/html.css\nhttp://mxr.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/source/layout/style/res/quirk.css\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
